   "about": "The conclusion assesses how long Japan could sustain war production using Inner Zone industry and stockpiles.",
   "summary": "The report estimates that the Inner Zone supplies most iron, steel, coal, salt, rice and transport capacity, while Japan Proper depends heavily on Korea, Manchuria and North China. It projects stockpiles of many southern raw materials through 1945, but identifies oil and several metals as continuing concerns. It argues that losing the southern territories alone would leave Japan able to continue fighting, whereas losing Manchuria and Korea would cripple its war economy.",
